Kubernetes

Kubernetes doesn’t run with swap. We should disable the swap memory from every machine that is part of cluster.
When we start the cluster API server starts running on the manager. It is the epic center of every communication. Whatever communication happens in the cluster, it will go thru the API server. Every worker node as well as manager an agent called kubelet will run.
 API servers communicate to kubelet. Kubelet keeps on sending the machine current state like how much CPU/Memory/Pod details to API server periodically. Then API server store all the data to etcd, which is key value data store. 
Admins interact or give instructions with manager using utility called kubectl, which is installed on manager. API server will check Authentication and Authorization. Then API server will inform the Scheduler in the manager. Scheduler behalf of API find the best node from etcd. Scheduler picks the best node and inform to API. Then API server will initiate a call to kubelet of best node and instruct the node to create container with given image. Every machine agent called kubelet container engine is running. Kubelet will instruct container engines to create containers. Then Container engine will do lift and shift. Container will respond back to kubelet. Then Kubelet will respond to API Server. API servers update the etcd, then to Admin. One more component called kubeproxy will run on every worker, which facilitates container to container communication. On the manager one more component called kube-controller manager, which will communicate to API server, also checking desired stage of node like node controlled, service controller, replica controller, endpoint controller
