Persistent Storage
•	Storage in Kubernetes cluster is known as persistent volume subsystem
•	NFS storage will not act of Kubernetes cluster
•	It is more or less like LVM and it has 3 major components
1.	Persistent Volume - PV
2.	Persistent Volume Claim - PVC
3.	Storage Classes – SC:- It is used for dynamic storage
•	Storage in the cluster visible as PV, but Pod cannot access PV directly 
•	We need to create PVC and pod connect to PVC and PVC connect to PV. PVC act as a ticket to PV. 
•	It is a one-to-one mapping; we will not be able to create single block for more than one Application
•	Size  PV/PVC size should not be more than Block storage size
•	Permission : PV permission should be match with PVC permission
1.	Read Write Many (RWX)
2.	Read Write One (RWO)
3.	Read Only Many (ROM)
•	One PV with 2 PVC with different permission not allowed
•	Data retain policy: If application is deleted 
•	Difference storage type support different permissions
