Cluster Role
If users have permission is in the whole cluster is known as Cluster Role. Cluster Role is attached to a Cluster. We have predefined cluster role (i.e. Cluster Admin Role. Edit. view)
Role
If users have permission is in any specific namespace is known as Role. Role is attached to a namespace
Refer :  https://github.com/networknuts/kubernetes/blob/master/ch-07-rbac/steps-for-user-authentication 

Creating Openssl key
	When manages  installing the Kubernetes a self-signed certificate authority is automatically created
	csr Certificate Singing Request

# openssl genrsa -out vinitha.key 2048
 
Converting key into .csr from his workstation machine
# openssl req -new -key vinitha.key -out vinitha.csr -subj "/CN=vinitha"

User submit his key and csr to CA (on manager)
# scp vinitha.key user.csr login@manager:
Root CA will convert .csr into .crt and send the .crt back to user
# openssl x509 -req -in vinitha.csr -CA /etc/kubernetes/pki/ca.crt -CAkey /etc/kubernetes/pki/ca.key   -CAcreateserial -out vinitha.crt -days 365

# scp user.crt login@workstation:

User will create a .kube directory under his home and copy the config file sent by root CA

User also needs to install kubectl on his workstation
# sudo snap install kubectl --classic

Once this is done root CA will create user credentials on Kubernetes manager and limit user to a namespace
dev, for this example
# kubectl config set-credentials vinita --client-certificate=vinita.crt --client-key=vinitha.key
# kubectl config set-context vinitha-context --cluster=kubernetes --namespace=dev --user=vinitha

Refer : https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/access-authn-authz/rbac/
